1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Pr Ivan Alexeievich Galitzine, steward 1684, *11.11.1656, +17.4.1729; m.ca 1699 Pss Anastasia Petrovna Prozorovskaya (*22.10.1665, +10.3.1729); They had issue:  A1. Pr Feodor, general-major 1753, *29.1.1700, +4.10.
2 CONC 1759; 1m: 22.8.1725 Maria Lvovna Naryshkina (*1703, +XI.1727), 1st cousin of Tsar Peter I; 2m: 1728 Anna Petrovna Izmailova (*1712, +2.6.1749); all children by 2m.  B1. Pr Nikolai, general-poruchik, *2.12.1728, +20.3.1780; m.8.10.
2 CONC 1749 Praskovia Ivanovna Shuvalova (*10.10.1734, +1802)  C1. Pr Feodor, chamberlain, curator of the Moscow University, *7.4.1751, +6.12.1827; 1m: 13.2.1783 Pss Praskovia Nikolaievna Repnina (*1763, +Smolensk 19.10.1784); 2m: 1786 V
2 CONC arvara Ivanovna Shipova (+Paris 14.12.1804); all children by 2m.  D1. Pr Nikolai, *1789, +26.12.1860; m.Anna Feodorovna Bakhmeteva (+1.2.1842)  D2. Pr Ivan, colonel, *29.2.1792, +19.8.1835  D3. Pr Feodor, dit Fifi, chamberlain, *6
2 CONC .4.1794, +16.10.1854  D4. Pr Alexander, chamberlain, member of the State Council (1852-64), *Moscow 29.7.1796, +St.Petersburg 12.11.1864; m.Moscow 15.5.1821 Css Nadezhda Ivanovna Kutaisova (*St.Petersburg 26.11.1796, +St.Petersbur
2 CONC g 15.2.1868)  E1. Pr Evgeni, *Moscow 11.2.1822, +drowned nr Kronstadt 17.6.1854  E2. Pss Alexandra, *Moscow 30.10.1823, +1918; m.St.Petersburg 12.5.1857 Illarion Nikolaievich Tolstoy (*28.9.1832, +15.4.1904), aide-de-camp of Tsar 
2 CONC Alexander II  F1. 
2 CONT ===Nadezhda Tolstaya, *1860, +Finland 1937; m.Alexander Sergeievich Taneyev (*17.1.1850, +7.2.1918), ober-hofmeister 
2 CONT G1. 
2 CONT ===Anna Taneyeva, lady-in-waiting and the closest friend of Empress Alexandra Feodorovna, wrote the famous memoirs about the Imperial family, *St.Petersburg 16.7.1884, +Helsinki 20.7.1964 as a nun; m.1907 (div 1917) Alexander Vasi
2 CONC lievich Vyrubov (*1880, +Kislovodsk 4.3.1919)===
