2 CONT
2 CONT Name	Prince Nikolai Nikolaevitch KASATKIN-ROSTOVSKY
2 CONT Gender	Male
2 CONT Birth?	1886	
2 CONT Marriage	1904	
2 CONT to Maria Fedorovna KAMENSKY
2 CONT Residence?		
2 CONT owners of the house 84, Moika emb.
2 CONT Death?	May 1918	
2 CONT Cause: assasinated by Bolsheviks
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince NIKOLAI K-R was the son of Prince Nikolai Fedorovich K-R (1848-1908), Acting State Councillor and Member of the Council of the Empire, and Nadezhda Karlovna de Montresor (1852-1917), a dau. of Karl Lukianovich de Montresor 
2 CONC and Nadezhda Fedorovna Poltoratskaia. He had the following siblings: 1) Princess Nadezhda Nikolaevna K-R (1873-1949) who married Nikolai Evgrafovich Mukhanov (1864-1933) 2) Prince Fedor Nikolaevich K-R (1875-1940) who m. 1stly Olg
2 CONC a Ermogenovna Khvoshchinskaia (1878-1952) and 2ndly Dina Nikitichna Kirova. 3) Princess Sofia Nikolaevna K-R (1877-1918) 4) Princess Aleksandra Nikolaevna K-R (1885-1973) who married Anatolii Dmitrievich Vsevolozhskii (1870-1927) 
2 CONC 5) Prince Georgii Nikolaevich K-R (1897-?) According to the "Almanach de St-Petersbourg 1913/14" p. 294, Prince Nikolai Nikolaevich K-R was the President of the "Uprava" of the District of Novoskolsk, Government of Kursk.
