2 CONT https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Nikolai_Kasatkin-Rostovsky_%28...
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Nikolai Nikolaevitch KASATKIN-ROSTOVSKY
2 CONT b.1886
2 CONT d.May 1918
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Prince Nikolai Nikolaevitch KASATKIN-ROSTOVSKY
2 CONT Gender Male
2 CONT Birth? 1886
2 CONT Marriage 1904
2 CONT to Maria Fedorovna KAMENSKY
2 CONT Residence?
2 CONT owners of the house 84, Moika emb.
2 CONT Death? May 1918
2 CONT Cause: assasinated by Bolsheviks
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince NIKOLAI K-R was the son of Prince Nikolai Fedorovich K-R (1848-1908), Acting State Councillor and Member of the Council of the Empire, and Nadezhda Karlovna de Montresor (1852-1917), a dau. of Karl Lukianovich de Montresor 
2 CONC and Nadezhda Fedorovna Poltoratskaia. He had the following siblings: 1) Princess Nadezhda Nikolaevna K-R (1873-1949) who married Nikolai Evgrafovich Mukhanov (1864-1933) '''2) Prince Fedor Nikolaevich K-R (1875-1940) who m. 1stly 
2 CONC Olga Ermogenovna Khvoshchinskaia (1878-1952) and 2ndly Dina Nikitichna Kirova.''' 3) Princess Sofia Nikolaevna K-R (1877-1918) 4) Princess Aleksandra Nikolaevna K-R (1885-1973) who married Anatolii Dmitrievich Vsevolozhskii (1870-
2 CONC 1927) 5) Prince Georgii Nikolaevich K-R (1897-?) According to the "Almanach de St-Petersbourg 1913/14" p. 294, Prince Nikolai Nikolaevich K-R was the President of the "Uprava" of the District of Novoskolsk, Government of Kursk.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From “Prince Fyodor Nikolaevich Kasatkin-Rostovsky - poet and officer,”  by Stanislav Minakov pl 04/21/2017 [http://www.stoletie.ru/territoriya_istorii/_my_krest_svoj_nesem_kak_nosili_pogony_451.htm link] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >In 1912, the prince's marriage to Olga Bogdanovna (Germogenovna) Khvoshchinskaya (1871 - 1952, Canada) was dissolved, which was concluded in June 1898. It is known about his daughter''' Marina (1900 - 1979'''), born in this marri
2 CONC age, but some sources name three more children: Irina (1906-1947), Cyril (1904-1980) and Nikolai (1908-1947). It was even reported about the last son that he took part in the Great Patriotic War and died in the camps in Semipalati
2 CONC nsk.
2 CONT
