1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sergei Iosifovich Trishatny (19 March [O.S. 7] 1865 — after April 21, 1920). Barrister, a Secretary of the board of the Union of Russian People (URP), a loyalist right-wing nationalist party, the most important[13]
2 CONC  among Black-Hundredist monarchist and antisemitic political organizations in the Russian Empire of 1905–1917.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known as the organizer of terroristic combat squads (Russian: боевые дружины) which shot and murdered political opponents of URP, from deputies of Duma to the left-wing functionaries. In 1907–08 following growing internal conflict
2 CONC s and power struggle in the URP Trishatny withdrew from his active participation in the Union.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trishatny_family
