2 CONC .G. KRISTI's nephew. Owner of the Kazatskoye * estate in the Kherson province. on the Dnieper, where he built a castle and bred grapes on the advice of a friend of the winemaker Lev Golitsyn. '' *. The "Cossack" form has become th
2 CONC e norm in Russian, while "Cossack" is the norm in Ukrainian. In the context of a conversation about the Ukrainian Cossacks, one can also find the "Cossack" in the Russian text. Gogol uses kOzak in the Russian text, and the form wi
2 CONC th "o" also got into foreign languages ​​and stuck there. Cossak. The modern settlement is called Kozatske. ' 
