2 CONT Mal'tsev, Sergei Ivanovich (17.II.1876+20.XII.1920).  Educated in the Naval Academy,  promoted to the Garde Equipage,  took part in the Russo~Japanese War (1904~1905),  retired (1905),  Gentleman of the Court,  joined the Army in 
2 CONC 1914 with the rank of Colonel,  Adjutant of the Commander~in~Chief of the South~Western Front (1914~1917).  Murdered by the Bolsheviks along with his wife and mother~in~law in Yalta.
2 CONT
