2 CONT Alexandra Alexandrovna von Pistohlkors (née Taneyeva; 8 November 1888 – 25 March 1968) was the younger daughter of noted Russian composer Alexander Taneyev and the sister of Anna Vyrubova. Her husband was Alexander Erikovich von P
2 CONC istohlkors, who was the stepson of Grand Duke Paul Alexandrovich of Russia.[citation needed] Like her sister, Alexandra was for a time a devotee of the starets Grigori Rasputin.
