1 NOTE {geni:about_me} D.V. and Marina Giri were the parents of Dr. George Anand Rurik Giri, OBE.  Her parents were Prince Fyodor Nikolaevich Kasatkin-Rostovsky and Olga Bogdanovna (Germogenovna) Khvoshchinskaya.  She “fled from Russia a
2 CONC t the time of the Revolution.”  Her second husband was Major Edmund Boothroyd Corby of the British War Office.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From “princes Kasatkin-Rostov“  [https://forum.svrt.ru/topic/11020-%D0%BA%D0%BD%D1%8F%D0%B7%D1%8C%D1%8F-%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%8B-%D1%80%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B5/ link] 
2 CONT
2 CONT *XXXII. 157.151 (from 1) knzh. Marina Fedorovna (06/23/1900, St. Petersburg, - 02/14/1979, London) Husband (married since 1919, Paris) Venkatagiriah Devorayadurg (1881-1960, Australia)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From “Prince Fyodor Nikolaevich Kasatkin-Rostovsky - poet and officer,”  by Stanislav Minakov pl 04/21/2017 [http://www.stoletie.ru/territoriya_istorii/_my_krest_svoj_nesem_kak_nosili_pogony_451.htm link] 
2 CONT
2 CONT >In 1912, the prince's marriage to Olga Bogdanovna (Germogenovna) Khvoshchinskaya (1871 - 1952, Canada) was dissolved, which was concluded in June 1898. It is known about his daughter''' Marina (1900 - 1979'''), born in this marri
2 CONC age, but some sources name three more children: Irina (1906-1947), Cyril (1904-1980) and Nikolai (1908-1947). It was even reported about the last son that he took part in the Great Patriotic War and died in the camps in Semipalati
2 CONC nsk.
