1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mikhail Mikhailovich Ossorguine, my first cousin, was a Russian Orthodox monk-priest in Alaska were he met and fell in love with an American woman. When he asked to be relieved of his monkhood so as to be allowed t
2 CONC o marry but kept as a priest as this was his vocation, his superiors refused. He then got married anyway and was forbidden by his superiors to officiate as a priest. He and his wife moved to Santa Fe, New Mexico, where he built a 
2 CONC little Orthodox church on his property and officiated as a priest anyway, defying his superiors. He was very much beloved by his parishioners, and his sister Ioulia Ossorguine moved from Paris to Santa Fe to be close to her brothe
2 CONC r. She is still living there, very old and blind and slowly going deaf. Mikhail and his wife had several children, two of whom I met briefly in 1984 - but alas I don't remember how many siblings in total they were nor do I remembe
2 CONC r all their names save for two.
