1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bezobrazov (Count Chernyshev~Bezobrazov), Vladimir Aleksandrovich (1893+15.IX.1956).  Volunteer (1914),  Orderly of General Bezobrazov (1914~1915), promoted to Ensign in Sapper Guards Regiment (31.XII.1915). Died i
2 CONC n Mexico.
2 CONT
2 CONT The General Vladimir Mihaïlovich Bezobrazov must be referring to him as "Chernyshev~Bezobrazov" here to differentiate between him and the other Bezobrazov's. Elsewhere, he refers to him simply as "Bezobrazov", which is the way he 
2 CONC and his brother Sergei were known in Russia. In 1896, Princess Orina Sergeevna Bagration~Moukhransky (née Coutess Chernyshev~Bezobrazov) and her cousin Count Zachary Alexandrovitch Tchernicheff~Besobrasoff wrote and published a ge
2 CONC nealogy of their family showing that the title and style of Count Chernyshev~Bezobrazov was to pass equally to all descendants, male and female, and not as has been suggested by primogeniture.
