2 CONT Bezobrazov, Vladimir Vladimirovich (6.II.1892 a.s.+16.X.1940). Eldest son of General Bezobrazov. Educated in the Corps of Pages, Page of Emperor Nicholas II, promoted to His Majesty's Hussar Guards Regiment (1912), served in the R
2 CONC egiment until placed in the Reserve of the Petrograd Military District (9.X.1917), took part in the World War (1914~1917). contused (1915), took part in the fighting against the forces of Petlura around Kiev in the force of Genera
2 CONC l Kipichev (20.XI-13.XII.1918). Emigrated from Russia and died in the Belgian Congo.
