1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Orlov, Aleksei Aleksandrovich (14.XII.1891+9.IV.1955).  Educated in the 1st Cadet Corps and the Nikolaevski Cavalry School,  promoted to His Majesty's Hussar Guards Regiment (1911),  awarded the Golden Sword (WWI),
2 CONC   transferred to the 7th Aviation "Division" (1917),  sent to the Eupatoria Military Flying School (5.X.1917),  member of the Special Service Company of the Volunteer Army guarding the Members of the Imperial Family in the Crimea 
2 CONC (1919),  sent to the Caucasian Army after the departure of the Imperial Family (III.1919) as a squadron commander in the Kabardin Horse Regiment.  Left Russia at the end of the Civil War and died in Rome.
